ment.yaml:168 --quote 'podSelector: {}' --counter \"Searched deployment.yaml and terraform for 0.0.0.0/0, ::/0 and extra egress rules; found only DNS, the proxy and a /28. Whether the cluster CNI enforces NetworkPolicy is not configured in this repo.\" --note \"Namespace-wide default-deny with named peers.\"\na check B08.2 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:35 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:secret:clinic-agent/*\"' --note \"One runtime role reads every clinic's EHR, payments and SMS secrets (and the _catalog secret). Combined with the model-supplied clinicId at executor.ts:63, there is a credential path to other tenants. IMDS is limited (http_tokens required, hop limit 1) but this cross-tenant credential reach remains.\"\na check B08.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' --note \"Tenant isolation is code only. The model chooses clinicId; no check that it is the caller's tenant or a sibling; it is used to build secret ids and the x-clinic-id header (ehr-mcp.ts:36,58). Network isolation is in NetworkPolicy, but tenant isolation has no infrastructure rule behind it.\"\na flag B08 --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --note \"model-supplied clinicId selects any tenant's credentials with no validation\"\n# B09\na check B09.1 --met unknown --evidence k8s/deployment.yaml:189 --quote 'matchLabels: { app: egress-proxy }' --note \"NetworkPolicy denies everything but the proxy, so default-deny is in the repo. The destination allowlist lives in the platform egress proxy, only described in a comment at deployment.yaml:160; its rules are not in this repo.\"\na check B09.2 --met yes --evidence k8s/deployment.yaml:169 --quote 'policyTypes: [\"Egress\", \"Ingress\"]' --counter \"Searched for 0.0.0.0/0, ::/0, hostNetwork, extra egress and ipv6 rules; none. Proxy enforced by Network