{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdrGouAYX3pKLtQMc3BX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch review of B06–B10 is finished and saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. It passes `validate_findings.py --fix --batch B06,B07,B08,B09,B10 --before-challenges` (\"Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.\"). All five items are gaps. I did not run challenges and added no other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity (G1) | gap | `checkApproval` (`src/tools/approvals.ts:60-82`) never compares `argsHash` or `agentInstanceId`. It never marks an approval used, so an approval can be replayed or reused with different arguments for its 900-second life. The args hash (`approvals.ts:29`) also drops nested keys. No permission or resource-state recheck happens before `tool.invoke`. A failing approval store does deny the action (B06.5 is yes). |\n| B07 Hard budgets (G2) | gap | The classifier model call (`src/agent/classifier.ts:45`) is outside every run budget and shared quota. Shared quotas are also charged only after the main model call returns. The six limits themselves are all set (B07.1 is yes). |\n| B08 Environment isolation (G2) | gap | The model chooses `clinicId` (`src/tools/executor.ts:63`), and it is used to pick secrets and the EHR clinic header. The runtime IAM role can read every clinic's secrets (`infra/terraform/iam.tf:35`). Tenant isolation is code-only. The NetworkPolicy is default-deny (B08.1 is yes). |\n| B09 Egress allowlist (G2) | gap | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83` fetches a URL taken from an unverified peer response header, with no allowlist, redirect or IP checks. The other outbound calls have no redirect or IP checks either. The proxy allowlist, per-resource limits and block alerts are outside the repo (B09.1, B09.4, B09.5 unknown). Direct egress is blocked by the NetworkPolicy for IPv4 and IPv6 (B09.2 is yes). |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image (G2) | gap | Images are digest-pinned and Cosign is v2.6.2. Signature checking happens only in the deploy workflow, and provenance is generated but never verified. No admission policy exists in the repo, so nothing enforces a signature in the cluster. |\n\nThe 11 prescan hits (B02, B11, E03, R13) belong to other batches, so I left them unresolved. The scope field in the findings file says so. I found no injection attempts in the repo.\n\nFor B08.1 I answered yes. The repo shows no EKS network-policy enforcement setting, so that is a caveat rather than a finding.\n\nI also left helper files in `agent/`: `brace-prescan.json`, `brace-inventory.json`, `brace-coverage-*.json` and `empty.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":92776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610},"output_tokens":794,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4cc3c69-55e0-473e-bfe4-b389a6e801c0","uuid":"648680c0-5938-40fb-ad87-435950ef092b","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:03:04.570Z","request_id":"req_011CfdrGoWMxvfhdxjRWAjF1"}
